{"id":1226,"date":"2021-03-19T01:50:31","date_gmt":"2021-03-19T01:50:31","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/?post_type=rdrcnews&#038;p=1226"},"modified":"2021-03-19T16:58:13","modified_gmt":"2021-03-19T16:58:13","slug":"meet-the-dfr-storefront-improvement-program-artists","status":"publish","type":"rdrcnews","link":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/rdrcnews\/meet-the-dfr-storefront-improvement-program-artists\/","title":{"rendered":"DFR Artist Commissioning Program Artists"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">Meet The Artists &#8211; Downtown Far Rockaway Artist Commissioning Program\/Storefront Improvement<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The CBO of the Rockaways partnered with <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.queenscouncilarts.org\/far-rockaway-artist-commissioning-program\">Queens Council on the Arts<\/a><\/span> (QCA) has launched the Downtown Far Rockaway (DFR) Artist Commissioning Program through grant-winning from the <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/site\/sbs\/neighborhoods\/storefront-improvement.page\">New York City Department of Small Business Services<\/a><\/span>. A democratized art commissioning project focused on placing artwork designed by local artists on solid rolldown gates of businesses located in Downtown Far Rockaway.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">This Initiative will help address the areas&#8217; negative perceptions by creating the opportunity to present post-COVID-19 DFR as a vibrant hub for the growth of art support cultures and as destinations to enjoy food and thriving local culture.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">The program has two components:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Artists will create temporary new works of public art to install on the roll down gates of designated downtown Far Rockaway businesses.<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The residency will include a public unveiling of the artwork open to the surrounding community. Queens Council on the Arts (QCA) is proud to be part of this program on behalf of downtown Far Rockaway.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Come meet the Artists and Panelist, Friday, March 26th, 12noon-2pm, at the CBO&#8217;s office, located at 1920 Mott Avenue, Far Rockaway, NY. <\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-1227 \" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist1.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"161\" height=\"241\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist1.jpeg 1000w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist1-200x300.jpeg 200w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist1-768x1150.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist1-684x1024.jpeg 684w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 161px) 100vw, 161px\" \/><\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Brandi Jones<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-1228 \" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"230\" height=\"230\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney.jpeg 1358w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney-150x150.jpeg 150w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney-300x300.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney-768x768.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-2-Brendan_McInerney-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 230px) 100vw, 230px\" \/><\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Brendan Mcinerney<\/span><br \/>\n&nbsp;<br \/>\n<img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-1229\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3Shenna.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"230\" height=\"288\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3Shenna.jpeg 1200w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3Shenna-240x300.jpeg 240w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3Shenna-768x960.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3Shenna-819x1024.jpeg 819w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 230px) 100vw, 230px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Shenna Vaughn<\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-1230\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"236\" height=\"236\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3.jpeg 1500w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3-150x150.jpeg 150w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3-300x300.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3-768x768.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/DFR-Artist-3-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 236px) 100vw, 236px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Stanislova Ivanova<\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Their creative, artistic synergy, will ensure the success of this exciting program! CONGRATULATION TO THE DFR WINNERS!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">For additional details on the DFR Storefront Improvement Program, email Valerie Stevens at <span style=\"c